{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.alfred.edu/student-life/career-development-center/index.cfm": {
      "title": "The Robert R. McComsey Career Development Center",
      "description": "The Robert R. McComsey Career Development Center | Alfred University Skip To Top Navigation Skip To Content Skip To Footer Apply Visit Request Info Give Search Search alfred.edu Search alfred.edu Menu Close Search alfred.edu Search alfred.edu About show submenu for About Alfred at a Glance History & Traditions Awards & Accolades Our Mission Alfred Community Institutional Research Campus Map Policies Academics show submenu for Academics Undergrad Majors & Minors Graduate Programs Colleges & Schools Off-Campus Programs Academic Support Summer & Winter Terms Academic Calendar Study Abroad Experiential Learning Honors Research Admissions & Aid show submenu for Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Graduate Transfer International Tuition & Fees Affording Alfred Financial Aid Admissions Counselors Student Life show submenu for Student Life Housing & Dining First Year Experience Campus Safety Clubs & Organizations Inclusivity Fitness & Recreation Health & Wellness Career Development Athletics show submenu for Athletics Official AU Saxons Saxon Hill Club & Intramural Sports Facility Hours Spirit Shop Pre-College Programs Information for Prospective Students Accepted Students Families & Parents Visitors Current Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Research & Business Partners Job Seekers High School Counselors Quick Links Request Info Apply Visit Blog News Events MyAU Directory Give Bookstore Libraries Our Promise The Robert R. McComsey Career Development Center Take charge of your career Welcome to the Robert R. McComsey Career Development Center at Alfred University! Our mission and values honor Abigail Allen, friend and mentor to generations of students, a strong supporter of co-education, and wife of Alfred University’s second president. Explore the many career-readiness resources we provide students, alumni, faculty, and employers. Resources for Students and Alums Your future goals are our number one priority. Whether you're ready to start your job search now or not quite sure where to go from here, we can help. Info for Students and Alums Resources for Employers Are you an employer interested in recruiting students who are well-rounded and knowledgeable about their field? Our office connects you to the right candidates for your open opportunities. Services for Employers Faculty and Staff If you are an AU faculty or staff member interested in partnering with our office for a classroom presentation or workshop, please contact us. Contact Us What Can I Do With This Major? The Career Development Center has purchased a subscription to What Can I Do With This Major? - an online career exploration tool for students. What Can I Do With This Major? is a website featuring 106 major profiles with information on common career paths, types of employers that hire in the field, and strategies to maximize opportunities. Links to professional associations, occupational outlook information, and job search resources are included. Get started video APEX (Applied Experiential Learning) Transform a good education into an extraordinary education! Juniors and Seniors can apply for funding to engage in work experience and study/research opportunities to enhance their career decision-making, increase their opportunities after graduation and inspire them to find their passions in life. Learn more about APEX. Learn More About APEX Career Fairs Career Fairs at Alfred University Find on- and off-campus employment opportunities at one of our career fairs. Explore these resources to learn more about these networking opportunities. Information on Career Fairs Thank You to our Employer Sponsors and Partners The Robert R. McComsey Career Development Center staff would like to express our sincerest gratitude to the employers who have joined us in our pursuit of providing the highest level of support to students entering the workforce following graduation from Alfred University. Without their support, we could not provide the robust catalog of resources available to our students and alumni. Become a Sponsor Parents, Families & Outcomes We provide a wide variety of services and programs to help students find their professional purpose and meaningful work. Parents and families can assist us with this goal through strategic networking, mentoring and more. Additional CDC Offerings Service Learning The goal of the Gary Horowitz Service Learning Program is to foster an environment of social responsibility and community engagement, and... Cheryl's Closet Cheryl’s Closet supports and empowers students by offering free professional attire in a boutique setting. Alumni Services The Robert R. McComsey Career Development Center offers ongoing support to alums. Contact us for more information about accessing our resources after graduating. Faculty / Staff Here's just a few people from our Career Development Team. See Full Career Development Team Previous Jessica Doner Excutive Director of Career Development & Advising Hannah Miles Assistant Director of Career Development Center and Career Coach & Advisor Em Cronin Employer Relations and Experiential Learning Coordinator Next Go to slide 1 Go to slide 2 More About the Robert R. McComsey Career Development Center Mission The Robert R. McComsey Career Development Center empowers students and alumni to find their professional purpose and meaningful work through informed decision-making, practical experience, and connection to the global community. Values We express our core value of professionalism through expertise, responsibility, empathy, and balance. Expertise encompasses our knowledge, skills and resources; expertise promotes positive connections with our stakeholders. Responsibility is reflected in our high level of dependability, integrity, and ethics; responsibility ensures the reliable delivery of services. Empathy is demonstrated through our approachability, attentiveness, and availability; empathy allows for individualized service to our diverse population. Balance is expressed in both our work and personal lives; balance supports our students and alumni to find fulfillment in their chosen paths. Follow Us For the latest news about internships, co-op opportunities, APEX grants, career fairs, resume critiques, mock interviews and so much more, follow our official social media accounts! Contact Us The Robert R. McComsey Career Development Center is conveniently located at the center of the Alfred University Campus in the Welcome Center, formerly known as Alumni Hall. We invite you to please stop by or email us directly to learn more about the services we offer Alfred students, alumni and employers. Email us: cdc@alfred.edu Latest Student Services Posts From The Spark The Spark is the official blog of Alfred University. Check our latest posts! See All Student Services Posts Previous You’re Headed to Alfred: Let’s Talk Housing for New Students Posted By Alfred University July 07, 2026 Finals Week at the Libraries: Study, Snack, Relax Posted By Alfred University May 07, 2026 Discover the Personal Librarian Program That Supports Student Success Posted By Alfred University February 27, 2026 Next Go to slide 1 Go to slide 2 Events at the CDC All Alfred Events Oct 22 AU Energy Conference October 22 | Golisano Institute, Rochester Institute of Technology Aug 27 MediaLab Workshop: Foundations in Media Production August 27 | Herrick Memorial Library, Computer Lab Feb 26 Spring 2026 Career & Grad School Fair February 26 | Joyce & Walton Family Center for Health & Wellness We'll Help You Find the Answers Contact Us Career Development Center Career Development Center 607-871-2164 cdc@alfred.edu Alumni Hall Jessica Doner Excutive Director of Career Development & Advising (607) 871-2174 doner@alfred.edu Follow CDC on Social 1 Saxon Drive Alfred, NY 14802 607-871-2111 Maps & Directions Emergency Information Request Info Visit Us Apply Now Top Information For Prospective Students Accepted Students Families & Parents Visitors Current Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Research & Business Partners Job Seekers High School Counselors Policies Privacy Policy Anti-Discrimination Policy Accessibility Title IX Top Copyright © 2026 Alfred University | Site Map Top"
    },
    "https://my.alfred.edu/index.cfm": {
      "title": "MyAU",
      "description": "MyAU | My Alfred University Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Home My Dashboard Resources Offices Quick Links Overview Email BannerWeb Canvas U:Drive Degree Works Handshake AU Report IT People Search Navigate Login Monday, Oct. 19, 2026 Useful Info Useful Info For Close this panel Students Student Service Center Email Activation Help (Info) My Printing Purchase My Printing Status Faculty/Staff Banner Administration Human Resources Business Office Web Request Form The Saxon Shop Miscellaneous AU Connect Info Technology Services Password Info Alfred Today (Submit Content) Facilities & Work Orders/Requests Open the search panel Close this panel Search Alfred University Go Menu MyAU Homepage AU Connect Fiat Festifall Wheel of Wow! $2 Movie Tuesdays Celebrate Alfred, Day of Service Open Mic Night Trunk or Treat at President Zupan's House Haunted Hayride Axe Throwing Pumpkin Sculpting with Eric Jones Wickham Farms The Rocky Horror Picture Show Pumpkin Smash Pumpkin Hunt Information Information Technology Services (ITS) Resources for Faculty/Staff and Students Need technology assistance? Visit Information Technology Services' Helpdesk portal by clicking the button below. You will need to sign in with your Alfred University email address and password to view it. In the portal you will find a knowledgebase where you can: find common solutions to IT problems, request service, as well as view currently open and/or closed requests. Helpdesk Portal Announcements What is Common Ground? Click to Open If you're a first-year or transfer student, you'll notice a class called Common Ground on your spring schedule. In this one-credit course, you'll have the kinds of discussions that we see as essential to your education -- about what's going on in the world, what kind of community we want to create, and how to have civil discourse across ideological boundaries. You'll get a chance to meet (and have meaningful conversation with) students with diverse academic interests, backgrounds, and beliefs. Classes only meet once a week for 50 minutes, so it won't add to your academic workload, but it will add value to your AU degree by developing your capacity to work well with others (and it is a university requirement). Classes meet either Wednesdays or Thursdays, 3:20 - 4:10. Because we don't want Common Ground to interfere with the rest of your academic program, we won't assign you to a particular section until you've had a chance to register for your other spring classes. If you have any questions about the Common Ground program, please contact Melissa Ryan, Professor of English, ryanm@alfred.edu . Posted by : ryanm Interested in obtaining funding for a research project? Click to Open Student proposals requesting Spring 2027 funding from the Alfred Research Grants for Undergraduate Students (ARGUS) program are due by midnight on Friday, November 20. Instructions for preparing and submitting a proposal, along with supporting application materials, can be found at the link below. Proposals that do not follow the required format will be returned without review. If you have questions, email Dr. Wallace at wallaced@alfred.edu . Link: ARGUS application information Posted by : wallaced Submit Announcement View more announcements Events Today Mon, Oct 19 Tomorrow Tue, Oct 20 Wed, Oct 21 Today There are no events posted for today. Tomorrow Class Ring Sales - Wear Your Pride! Click to Open 11:00 AM - 3:00 PM Powell 2nd floor View more details for  Class Ring Sales - Wear Your Pride! Class Ring Sales - Wear Your Pride! Click to Open 11:00 AM - 3:00 PM Powell Main Lobby View more details for Class Ring Sales - Wear Your Pride! Wed, Oct 21 Celebrate International Education Week! Click to Open 10:15 AM - 3:15 PM Powell 2nd floor View more details for Celebrate International Education Week! Ceramic Pumpkin Carving Click to Open 5:30 PM - 7:30 PM Mcmahon 239 View more details for  Ceramic Pumpkin Carving Submit an Event View more events Alfred Today Canvas Tip of the Week:  Place all Quiz Questions on One Page Click to Open ITS is pleased to highlight Canvas tools and features that can help faculty and students achieve their goals.  This week's tip is: Place All Quiz Questions on One Page When creating a Quiz in Canvas, you have the ability to place all questions on one page (this is a default setting).  This choice is helpful for students who struggle with slow internet connections, as they do need to wait for multiple pages to load.  It also reinforces good habits and reduces text anxiety by allowing students to check their answers before submitting.  Instructions are included in the guide below. Link: Canvas Quiz Options Submitted by : Meghanne Freivald AI Open Mic Conversation - October 21, 12:30 - 1:00pm Click to Open An AI Open Mic Conversation will be held over Zoom on Wednesday, October 21, from 12:30 to 1 pm. This is an opportunity for faculty and staff to share their experiences with AI in a collaborative, informal setting. Participants will also have the opportunity to ask each other questions. The conversation will be guided by ITS staff and members of the AI Faculty Development Working Group, but there will be no formal presentation; the goal is to foster discourse on the topic of AI and learn from each other.  The Zoom link is provided below (meeting ID:  943 9399 0944, passcode:  554192). Link: AI Open Mic Conversation - October 21 Submitted by : Meghanne Freivald Universal Design for Learning (UDL) Drop-in Hours Click to Open On Monday, October 19, from 10:30am to 12:00pm, the Universal Design for Learning (UDL) Task Force will be hosting UDL Drop-in Hours. Faculty may stop by to seek assistance with applying UDL principles in their courses. Universal Design for Learning is the practice of creating learning experiences appropriate for all students, regardless of learning differences or diversity factors. The goal of UDL is to remove barriers to learning. Faculty who visit the drop-in hours may choose to focus on one of the following areas: - Applying UDL principles to a syllabus - Applying UDL principles to an assignment - Applying UDL principles to a Canvas course - Increasing the accessibility of electronic materials - A self-directed UDL goal related to teaching and course delivery UDL Drop-in Hours will be held in Scholes 218. If seeking assistance with a syllabus or assignment, please bring two paper copies. Please bring your laptop if seeking assistance with Canvas, digital accessibility, or another goal involving technology. Link: Universal Design for Learning Submitted by : Meghanne Freivald Last day to Withdraw Click to Open Don't forget Tuesday, Oct. 20, is the last day to withdraw from a class that meets all semester.  Be sure to fill out the form and obtain the necessary signatures before submitting to the Registrar's office at registrar@alfred.edu . Link: Course Withdrawal Form Submitted by : Alex Holbrook 2027-2028 Tuition Exchange Application Deadline is October 30, 2026 Click to Open Faculty and Staff - the Tuition Exchange Export Application deadline is October 30, 2026. If your child is planning to begin college (or transfer to another college) next year, 2027-2028 you may wish to explore the schools participating in the Tuition Exchange (TE) Program. RENEWAL TE Export applications are also subject to the deadline of October 30, 2026. Please read the attached TE Information Memo for application procedures and details on the program. Two application forms are required: The AU TE Export Application must be completed online at the TE website using the EZ-App: https://tuitionexchange.o... The AU Human Resources (HR) TR/TE form (please return to the HR office for approval at humanresources@alfred.edu ). Attachment: Tuition Exchange Community Memo Link: Tuition Exchange Export Application Submitted by : Barbara Landries October is Domestic Violence Awareness Month Click to Open Domestic and dating violence are prevalent in all communities, including college communities. One in five college students experienced dating or domestic violence in the last year. At Alfred University, we are committed to serving all students who are experiencing violence, including domestic and dating violence. If you are experiencing violence in your relationship or feel that you want help, please use the website, AU Report It, to report to the Title IX Office. During the month, Alfred University's Rape Crisis Advocate, Christa, will visit campus to provide information to students. She will be in the Powell Campus Center on October 9th, 16th, 19th, 20th, 22nd, 23rd, and 26th. If you want to meet with Christa while she's on campus, please contact carroll@alfred.edu to be connected. Link: AU Report It Submitted by : Michelle Carroll The Foreign Language Placement Exam (Tuesday, October 27, 2026) Click to Open The Foreign Language Placement Exam is an online test that is administered in person with proctoring. Online exams can be taken in French, German, Spanish, Italian, and Chinese. Students must PREREGISTER by emailing Prof. Kerry Kautzman ( kautzmka@alfred.edu ). In the email, include the language (French, German, Spanish, Italian, and Chinese) in which you would like to be tested. Modern Languages will offer this test on Tuesday, October 27th from 5:00 - 6:10 p.m. in Seidlin 016. You must pre-register by Tuesday, October 27th 2:00 p.m. Bring your student ID with you to the exam! Who should take a Placement Exam? Students who have taken more than two years of French, German, Spanish, Italian, or Chinese in high school and who intend to take the same language at AU should take the exam in that language. Students who are bilingual or native speakers of French, German, Spanish, Italian, or Chinese (or who have spoken the language at home) should take the exam in that language. Who does NOT need to take a Placement Exam? Students who are planning to take French, German, Spanish, Italian, or Chinese in college but have NOT studied that language in High School (or spoken it at home) do not need to take an exam. They should start by taking 101 in their chosen language. Students who wish to demonstrate proficiency in a language OTHER THAN French, German, Spanish, Italian, or Chinese should contact Prof. Kerry Kautzman ( kautzmka@alfred.edu ) about procedures for taking a Placement Exam through another institution. PLEASE NOTE: The Foreign Language Placement Exam is online but only offered in person on specific dates during each semester. You must register ahead of time. There is a limit of 15 for each session. Submitted by : Janet McClain Let's Talk About The Cornell 7 Click to Open Safe Space Conversation - Cornell Conversation Thursday, October 22 | 11:20 a.m.-12:10 p.m. Susan Howell Room Join us for a small, informal Safe Space Conversation focused on creating a welcoming environment for dialogue and reflection following recent events at Cornell University. Michelle Carroll will facilitate the conversation, with Christa also joining us. This gathering is an opportunity to come together, listen, ask questions, share perspectives, and engage in meaningful conversation with one another. The goal is to create a space where participants can talk openly, thoughtfully, and respectfully while learning from different perspectives. Lunch will be provided. Space and food are planned for the first 25 participants to RSVP/register. RSVP through AU Connect! We hope you will join us for this important conversation. Attachment: Let's Talk About The Cornell 7 Link: https://youtu.be/BuDNGtf0L5Q Submitted by : Angie Taylor 9th Annual Leaf Rake by AU Women's Basketball Click to Open Alfred University Women's Basketball will be hosting our 9th annual Community Leaf Rake on Sunday, Nov. 1 from 9:00am-12:30pm. Available for anyone residing in the Alfred area! Please contact moskowitz@alfred.edu for more information. *This is on a first come, first serve basis. Availability is limited!* Submitted by : Michael Moskowitz Join Alfred University Concert Band! Click to Open Looking for an opportunity to make music, meet new people, and be part of a fun and engaging ensemble? Join the Alfred University Concert Band for the Spring 2027 semester! The Concert Band brings musicians together to rehearse and perform a variety of exciting concert band repertoire. Whether you're looking to continue playing your instrument or get back into music after some time away, this is a great opportunity to make music with others in a welcoming and collaborative environment. Rehearsal Schedule: Tuesdays and Thursdays 5:20-6:50 PM Performance: One concert at the end of the Spring 2027 semester With just one concert at the end of the semester, the Concert Band offers a rewarding musical experience. Come be part of the music this spring! We look forward to making music with you in the Alfred University Concert Band! Questions? Contact Dr. Mason St. Pierre for more details. Submitted by : Mason St. Pierre Interested in obtaining funding for a research project? Click to Open Student proposals requesting Spring 2027 funding from the Alfred Research Grants for Undergraduate Students (ARGUS) program are due by midnight on Friday, Nov. 20. Instructions for preparing and submitting a proposal, along with supporting application materials, can be found at the link below. Proposals that do not follow the required format will be returned without review. If you have questions, email Dr. Wallace at wallaced@alfred.edu . Link: ARGUS application information Submitted by : Desmond Wallace Submit Content Current Issue News Alfred University to welcome regional high school students for AUEnergy outreach event October 19, 2026 Alfred University will welcome regional high school students to campus on Oct. 29 for an opportunity to explore electrical and renewable energy engineering through demonstrations, laboratory visits, and conversations with current engineering students in those fields. Alfred University business students provide consultation for Westchester Children’s Chorus October 16, 2026 Two Alfred University students worked with the Westchester Children’s Chorus (WCC) on a consulting project designed to help the organization better understand its competitive landscape and identify opportunities for growth. Mechanical engineering faculty Mehdi Kabir  honored for editorial contributions to journal October 14, 2026 Mehdi Kabir, assistant professor of mechanical engineering in Alfred University’s Inamori School of Engineering, has been named recipient of the Springer Nature Editor of Distinction Award for 2026. Alfred University sophomore gains experience in research through NSF-funded S-STEM program October 12, 2026 Alfred University students are gaining hands-on research experience, exploring career possibilities, and building connections through a National Science Foundation S-STEM program focused on ceramic and glass engineering. View more press releases 1 Saxon Drive, Alfred, NY 14802 Information Desk 607-871-2111 Website Feedback Questions/Comments Directories Phone Directory Site Map Administration People Search Trustees Campus Info Hours of Operation How Do I... Parking & Transportation Getting To and From AU Campus Map Student Life Join a Club Recreation Campus Jobs Community Research Tools Academic Calendar Libraries Email Bannerweb Canvas Quick Tour of MyAU Emergency Information Privacy Policy Anti-Discrimination Policy Accessibility Sexual Misconduct & Title IX Copyright © 2026 Alfred University Alfred University E-News Alfred University Facebook Alfred University Twitter Alfred University YouTube Alfred University Instagram Alfred University Linkedin Alfred University Social Media Directory Back to Top"
